### Registro (sempre cria um CLIENT)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Registro com o mesmo e-mail novamente -> 409
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Registro com corpo inválido -> 400
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### Login (guarda o token na variável "token")
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Login com senha incorreta -> 401
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Endpoint protegido sem token -> 401
GET {{host}}/anything

### Endpoint protegido com token (404 significa que o token foi aceito, pois ainda não existe essa rota)
GET {{host}}/anything
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
